{
  "_note": "TBT budget: 200 ms for /ar; /ar/consultations/doctors 230 ms; /ar/c 340 ms (measured 2026-10-23 on a production build, applied/devtools throttling as in CI; local runs reproduce the CI report). Cause found: a loading.tsx on a static/ISR page makes the cached HTML carry the skeleton plus a swap script, so the page hydrates twice. Removing it from /ar/consultations/doctors took its TBT from a median of 313 ms to 158-201 ms (14 runs, 117-264); the 230 covers the run-to-run spread above 200. On /ar/c the same removal took TBT from 319 to 208 ms but made Time to Interactive unstable in CI (6057 ms against the 5500 budget in .github/lighthouse-budget.json; 2 of 6 local runs above 5500, the app bootstrap script requested ~1.1 s late), so /ar/c keeps its loading.tsx and its measured TBT: median 300-319 ms locally, 278-329 ms in CI, i.e. 129 ms above 200 at the worst CI median, plus 10 ms margin = 340. Lower /ar/c back to 200 when the 24 client product cards (generated ProductCard) and the client CoreShell stop hydrating on it. See docs/design/QUALITY_STANDARDS.md section 2.",
